            <ArticleTitle>Flunarizine in the treatment of headache with or without neurological symptoms.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>141-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Flunarizine was given in daily doses of 10 mg for periods of two to four months to 176 patients suffering from various types of headache. The symptoms were improved in 82% of the cases treated. No differences emerged among the various types of headache reported by the patients or in relation to the presence or absence of neurological involvement or its type.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
